# cuttle stealth-chromium patch #62 - persona CSS system colours and fonts.
#
# Source: chromium 154.0.8037.57
#   third_party/blink/renderer/core/layout/layout_theme.cc
#   third_party/blink/renderer/core/layout/layout_theme_font_provider_default.cc
#
# Chrome on Linux resolves the CSS system colours from Chromium's stock palette
# (ui/color/color_provider_utils.cc CompleteDefaultCssSystemColorDefinition).
# Chrome on Windows and on macOS each replace part of it with platform values,
# so a Linux build behind either persona answers keywords like no real browser:
# on Windows its red ActiveText fires CreepJS's hasKnownBgColor, which a real
# Windows browser does not; on macOS its Highlight, HighlightText and the light
# SelectedItem pair differ. The values and their sources are in the comment on
# CuttlePersonaSystemColor(); every one was measured on real Chrome 154, light
# and dark on the Mac, light on Windows 11.
#
# Both switch sites in layout_theme.cc still exist on 154. The live one in
# production is SystemColorFromColorProvider(): every renderer gets a colour
# provider, and DefaultSystemColor() is reached only in web tests or for
# keywords the provider does not carry (SelectedItem among them). The override
# sits in SystemColor(), ahead of both, so it needs no second copy.
#
# The Windows persona's menu, small-caption and status-bar system fonts are
# Segoe UI 12px, from the OS, where the Linux build answers Arial 16px. The Mac
# answers Arial 16px for all six keywords, as the Linux build already does.
diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/layout/layout_theme.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/layout/layout_theme.cc
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/layout/layout_theme.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/layout/layout_theme.cc
@@ -21,7 +21,12 @@
 
